# Security headers for the static client.
#
# These have to live here rather than in the Worker: with no `run_worker_first` in
# wrangler.jsonc, Cloudflare's asset server answers /broadcast.html, /watch.html and
# /earthseed.js directly and the Worker never sees those requests. (The Worker sets the
# same headers on the responses it does serve, e.g. "/".)
#
# THE POLICY LINES BELOW ARE GENERATED. `script-src` carries a sha256 for each inline
# <script> block in the pages, so editing a page — even its whitespace — invalidates them,
# and a stale hash does not fail loudly: the browser just refuses the script and the page
# does nothing. After touching any page in simple/, run:
#
#     node scripts/csp-hashes.mjs --write
#
# and run it without --write to check for drift before deploying.
#
# ENFORCED since 12 Aug 2026 (it shipped Report-Only first). Verified clean on Chromium and on
# WebKit 18.2 — the Safari 18 engine — because the risk was never Chrome: it was Safari
# disagreeing about hashed inline import maps or the worklet, which would break broadcasting on
# iOS with no console to look at. Both were checked directly: inline blocks execute under their
# hashes, and the worklet loads from a real file.
#
# `report-uri` is deliberately kept on the ENFORCED policy, so anything blocked on a browser we
# could not test still announces itself: `npx wrangler tail` shows /api/csp-report hits.
# Rollback is ENFORCE=false in scripts/csp-hashes.mjs + --write + deploy, which returns to
# reporting without blocking.
#
# `connect-src` is intentionally OPEN so that anyone can run a relay fleet on their own domain.
# That is a product requirement, not an oversight, and it costs little here: see the long note in
# scripts/csp-hashes.mjs for why (no script-injection sink exists in this client, and a relay only
# ever receives ciphertext). `script-src` is the control doing the real work, and Trusted Types
# keeps the no-sinks property enforced rather than merely observed.
/*
  # BEGIN generated policy
  Content-Security-Policy: script-src 'self' 'sha256-7fFJleZc815CALN3PfPMsYa6Qz0a0rce/C4FxOk3/zU=' 'sha256-/6+IyRllCt1Y75MNVZxrbWl18DUUChxSYKPODBQ2Vhs=' 'sha256-JCWAMn2pbmcJ89ksB/yW3efkkVZYIE7LtjDSTPgDF20=' 'sha256-sTYgfQK0g22fa73j8zdiZu5nPo2iXzr+QXxAF+ctaBs=' 'sha256-krqDlEnSdcLBnzFf7TsheImLZszyK/vZsqy44KMSelA=' 'sha256-2NCGmuIoDuwm1ymyrz9aZQPQLyOuKpzUeHaX4HOwpYE='; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; require-trusted-types-for 'script'; trusted-types 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; report-uri /api/csp-report
  # END generated policy
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
